speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to the standing orders of the House, I want to table a petition signed by 4,700 residents of various provinces in Canada. It says:
WHEREAS Interpol, an international police agency, obtains information on Canadian people;
WHEREAS Interpol gives that information to its fascist or communist members;
WHEREAS the personal integrity of each Canadian citizen must be protected against such actions;
THEREFORE the undersigned humbly ask your Honourable House to agree to break all relations with Interpol until an investigation by the government of Canada is completed or legislation passed to forbid the submission of information on Canadian citizens to fascist and communist countries by Interpol
And the undersigned will continue to urge you.
